## The Pharmacy — the big call

The auto `PHARMACY` disk culled the entire 3497-cell room. **I opened it as customer space**, because the drawing says so:

- The room's only interior boundary is one 1.03-pt partition traced from a single PDF stroke, and its east end leaves a **24.5 pt (2.2 m) archway** between the wall stub at (231.2,588.8) and the Floral case corner at (230.9,613.3) — **no door leaf, no swing arc**, while this guide *does* draw its doors (the deli staff double door, the Floral case doors, the frozen-case doors).
- "Pharmacy" is set in the same large red department type as Frozen Foods / Dairy / Market / Seafood / Produce / Floral; the OTC wing (First Aid, Laxatives, Cough/Cold, Diabetic, Nutrition, Diet, Vitamins) is printed directly north of it.
- I traced the pre-seal route out: east through the archway, along y≈596–604 between the display block `[255,574.9,270.1,601.1]` and the Floral case's open-door arcs, into the front alley. Two inclusions restore the room and that bay.

This is the store-24 failure mode, so flagging it explicitly: **if the auditor reads that room as a dispensary, the fix is to swap those two inclusions for an exclusion** — the evidence is written into the entry names.

